
#----------------------------- Global Properties ----------------------------#

/outputDir:bin/$(Platform)/Content
/intermediateDir:obj/$(Platform)
/platform:Windows
/config:
/profile:HiDef
/compress:False

#-------------------------------- References --------------------------------#

#---------------------------------- Content ---------------------------------#

# Everything here is built straight out of the Testbed's content directory, so there is one copy of each
# shader, texture and dome in the repository and a change reaches every executable at once (the map editor
# does the same). The one exception is the logo below, which is the Game's alone and lives in Images/logo
# beside its master — the same "build it where it already is" rule, pointed at a different directory.

# The overlay's font (FPS). The same description the Testbed's overlay uses, so the two read alike.
#begin ../../Testbed/Content/Fonts/segoeui.spritefont
/importer:FontDescriptionImporter
/processor:FontDescriptionProcessor
/processorParam:PremultiplyAlpha=True
/processorParam:TextureFormat=Color
/build:../../Testbed/Content/Fonts/segoeui.spritefont;Fonts/segoeui.spritefont

# The 2D logo the game opens on (#454) — the game's first and only bitmap asset, 2048 x 1267 RGBA straight
# alpha, cut out and trimmed to the drawing (Images/logo/README.md says how it was made and what must not be
# quietly undone). Loaded as "Images/Logo" and drawn by SplashPage, pixel for pixel at the owner's resolutions.
#
# PremultiplyAlpha=True is what BlendState.AlphaBlend wants and what makes a fade a plain scale on Color;
# loading the PNG with Texture2D.FromStream instead would skip it and fringe every edge.
#
# TextureFormat=Color, uncompressed, is a decision and not a default left standing: 2048 x 1267 x 4 is 10.4 MB
# in the .xnb (/compress:False above), which is what lands beside the exe. What it costs the DOWNLOAD was
# measured rather than reckoned from that figure, and the reckoning ("roughly 80 MB") was wrong: the file is
# mostly transparent black and deflates to about 2.6 MB, so a local self-contained publish went from 68.3 MB
# to 70.9 MB zipped. Compressed (BC3) would be a quarter of the on-disk size, but the height is not divisible
# by four, so the file would have to be padded or resized first, and block compression on this logo's large
# smooth gradients is exactly the case where banding shows. Padding to 1268 rows is the cheap experiment if
# the size is ever worth attacking. No mipmaps: the picture is only ever drawn at 1:1 or scaled DOWN through
# a bilinear sampler, and at the common half scale (1080p) that sampler is already an exact 2 x 2 box; a
# chain would add a third to the size for a softer picture at 1:1.
#begin ../../Images/logo/bs3d-logo-2048.png
/importer:TextureImporter
/processor:TextureProcessor
/processorParam:ColorKeyColor=255,0,255,255
/processorParam:ColorKeyEnabled=False
/processorParam:GenerateMipmaps=False
/processorParam:PremultiplyAlpha=True
/processorParam:ResizeToPowerOfTwo=False
/processorParam:MakeSquare=False
/processorParam:TextureFormat=Color
/build:../../Images/logo/bs3d-logo-2048.png;Images/Logo.png

